+### Sharing
+
+The owner of a list invites people with a link, and each person who accepts becomes a member with a role:
+
+| | owner | editor | viewer | no access |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Read the list, its tasks, tags, comments, activity and members | yes | yes | yes | 404 |
+| Create, change and delete tasks, comment on them | yes | yes | 403 | 404 |
+| Rename or delete the list, create, list and revoke invitations, remove members | yes | 403 | 403 | 404 |
+
+A user with no access to a list gets the same 404 as for one that does not exist, on the list and on its tasks and
+comments; a member who lacks the right gets `403 { "error": "forbidden" }`, before anything in the body is checked.
+Every right is checked where the list is read, so a task is always reached through its own list.
+
+| Method and path | Body | Answers |
+|---|---|---|
+| `POST /api/lists/:id/invitations` | `{ "role": "viewer" or "editor", "expires_in_hours"? }` | 201 `{ "id", "token", "url", "role", "expires_at", "created_at" }`; 400 for another role, or hours that are not a number above 0 and at most 720 (72 if omitted); owner only |
+| `GET /api/lists/:id/invitations` | | 200 `[{ "id", "role", "expires_at", "created_at" }]`: the invitations still pending, never their token; owner only |
+| `DELETE /api/lists/:id/invitations/:invitationId` | | 204: its link stops working; 404 if it is not pending; owner only |
+| `POST /api/invitations/:token/accept` | | 200, the list, with the caller's new `role`; 404 `{ "error": "invitation not found" }` |
+| `GET /api/lists/:id/members` | | 200 `[{ "id", "username", "role" }]`: the owner (role `owner`) first, then the members in the order they joined; any member |
+| `DELETE /api/lists/:id/members/:userId` | | 204; 400 for the owner, 404 for a user who is not a member; owner only |
+
+The invitation link, `url`, is `<origin>/#invite=<token>`. The origin is the `BASE_URL` environment variable when it
+is set (do set it behind a proxy or TLS, e.g. `BASE_URL=https://lists.example.com`), else `http://` and the `Host` of
+the request. The token is in the fragment, which browsers do not send, so it stays out of server logs and `Referer`
+headers; the page reads it, and accepts the invitation once the person is signed in or has signed up.
+
+- The token (32 random bytes) is shown once, in the answer that creates the invitation; only its SHA-256 hash is
+  stored. Lose the link and revoke the invitation to create another.
+- An invitation is single use: accepting it uses it up. It stops working when accepted, revoked or expired, and a
+  token that is unknown, expired, revoked or used all get the same 404.
+- If the owner, or someone who is already a member, accepts an invitation, they get the list as it is: their role
+  does not change and the invitation stays pending.
+- A role cannot be changed, and a member cannot leave: the owner removes the member and invites them again.
+- Removing a member unassigns their tasks in that list and cancels their reminders.
+
